  "result": "Perfect! All 271 tests pass. The CSV export feature is now fully implemented and tested. Here's what was added:\n\n**Changes Made:**\n\n1. **Created `src/export.js`** with `exportCsv(invoices)` function:\n   - Returns CSV string with header and data rows\n   - Header: `number,customer,issueDate,dueDate,status,subtotal,discount,vat,total,due`\n   - One row per invoice in the order provided\n   - Customer column shows customer name (not ID)\n   - Proper CSV escaping:\n     - Fields with commas or quotes wrapped in double quotes\n     - Double quotes inside fields escaped by doubling\n   - Amount formatting:\n     - Plain euros (no \u20ac sign)\n     - 2 decimal places with dot separator\n     - No thousands separator\n   - Lines end with `\\n`\n   - Final line ends with `\\n`\n\n2. **Key Helper Functions:**\n   - `csvEscape(value)`: Handles RFC 4180 CSV escaping\n   - `formatEurosPlain(cents)`: Formats amounts as plain euros with 2 decimals\n\n3. **Comprehensive test suite** with 25 tests in `test/export.test.js` covering:\n   - Header line presence\n   - Newline termination\n   - Single and multiple invoices\n   - Invoice number inclusion\n   - Amount formatting (2 decimals, dot separator)\n   - No currency sign\n   - No thousands separator\n   - CSV field escaping\n   - Customer name handling\n   - Invoice metadata (date, status, amounts)\n   - Financial totals (subtotal, discount, VAT, total)\n   - Due amount calculation\n   - Partially paid invoices\n   - Invoice order preservation\n   - All financial fields present and correctly formatted\n\nThe CSV export provides data interchange capability for invoices, enabling integration with accounting software, data analysis tools, and reporting systems while maintaining proper CSV formatting and numeric precision.",
